- B-V (color index): Indicates star temperature and spectral type; giants often have different color indices compared to dwarfs of the same spectral class.  
- SpType (spectral type): Spectral classification often includes luminosity class (V = main sequence/dwarf, III = giant, II = bright giant); this is the most direct indicator of giant status.  
- Amag (absolute magnitude): Intrinsic brightness; giants have lower (brighter) absolute magnitudes than dwarfs of the same spectral type.  

